    "body": "<p>Learn how to use Klaviyo’s campaign planner to create a personalized campaign plan. The campaign planner will populate your campaign calendar with placeholders after you provide information about your brand.</p>\n<p>Placeholders on the calendar are not actual draft campaigns. They are informational guides to inspire campaign creation. </p>\n<p>You can use a campaign plan to help determine:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>The type of content to send</li>\n<li>How frequently you send to subscribers</li>\n<li>What channels to use for different content (Email/SMS)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"h_01JS57ANGQ20XSKG7TTPJW5Y6B\">Create a campaign plan</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>Navigate to the <strong>Campaigns</strong> tab.</li>\n<li>Click the calendar icon in the top right to access the campaign calendar.<br>\n\n<img src=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/article_attachments/36126806274331\" alt=\"\" width=\"186\" height=\"106\">\n</li>\n<li>Click <strong>Plan campaigns</strong> above the calendar.</li>\n<li>On the first step of the planner, answer the questions about your business.<br>\n\n<img src=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/article_attachments/36126863099291\" alt=\"\" width=\"624\" height=\"391\">\n</li>\n<li>Click <strong>Next</strong> to generate a plan preview based on your answers.</li>\n<li>View the preview calendar with the newly added campaign placeholders. Here you can edit the types of campaigns you want on your calendar and the frequency at which you’ll send them.</li>\n<li>If you’re satisfied with the planner calendar, click <strong>Add to calendar </strong>at the top.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>You’ll now see the placeholders added to your calendar alongside any actual campaigns you have.</p>\n<h2 id=\"h_01JS57ANGQWGVVJRHKX0ZXX4MX\">Edit a campaign plan</h2>\n<p>The campaign planner preview shows 3 types of campaigns in the <em>Content types</em> section:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<strong><strong>Customer education</strong></strong><br>\nContent that shares tips or guides with customers.</li>\n<li>\n<strong>Product feature</strong><br>\nContent that highlights new releases or features.</li>\n<li>\n<strong>Promotion</strong><br>\nContent that provides details on an upcoming deal.\n<ul>\n<li>The date you want placeholders of this content type to start appearing on the calendar.</li>\n<li>How frequently you want placeholders of this content type to appear.</li>\n<li>Which channel(s) you want to include (Email, SMS, or both).<br>\n<ol>\n<li>Click <strong>Save</strong>.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>You can add or delete content types from your plan:</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<br>\n<img src=\"https://lh7-rt.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXcyVpcDqRFuAlkB4JtMVLL7EJsHyeO1C3CaYTfkiwL0yoc7_o3_vAJwQDOSYMUU0amODyBe5ncW6JBAKGwH23alBPm-OoXt1s-UZjOKSDUVVLfIN1y1q9b-YcWdNjVbGZClrl82?key=GIJmn3vylDRYZkJBVV0rGxyM\" alt=\"\" width=\"624\" height=\"493\">\n<p>To edit the content types:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>In the <em>Content types</em> section, click the <strong>edit (pencil) icon</strong>.</li>\n<li>Change one or more of the following:</li>\n</ol>\n</li>\n<li>Click the <strong>plus icon</strong> to add a content type to the plan.</li>\n<li>Click the <strong>trash can icon</strong> to delete a content type from the plan.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"h_01JS57ANGQPV5JDKTF40W6F6RB\">Show or hide all placeholders</h2>\n<p>After creating the placeholder calendar, placeholders will automatically show on your calendar view.</p>\n<p>To hide the placeholders:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Click the <strong>action icon (3 dots) </strong>above the campaign calendar.</li>\n<li>Select <strong>Add calendar</strong>.</li>\n<li>Click the <strong>X </strong>next to <strong>Campaign planner</strong>. This will hide the placeholders from your calendar view, but won’t delete them.</li>\n<li>Click <strong>Save</strong>.<br>\n\n<img src=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/article_attachments/36126806283035\" alt=\"\" width=\"552\" height=\"364\">\n<p>To show the placeholders again:</p>\n</li>\n<li>Click the <strong>action icon (3 dots) </strong>above the campaign calendar.</li>\n<li>Select <strong>Add calendar</strong>.</li>\n<li>From the dropdown, choose <strong>Campaign planner</strong>.</li>\n<li>Click <strong>Save</strong>.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2 id=\"h_01JS57ANGRJGGWCYAY6VMG6Z6F\">Create a campaign from a placeholder</h2>\n<p>To create a campaign using a placeholder:</p>\n<ol>\n<ol>\n<li>Click on the placeholder on the calendar to show a pre-built draft.<br>\n\n<img src=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/article_attachments/36126867048859\" alt=\"\" width=\"624\" height=\"464\">\n</li>\n<li>If you’re happy with the pre-built name, description, and audience, click <strong>Use this draft</strong> to open the campaign editor for this message to edit further.</li>\n<li>For more options, click the <strong>action icon (3 dots) </strong>and select one of the following:</li>\n</ol>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<strong><strong>Clone previous campaign</strong></strong><br>\nChoose an existing campaign to replace the placeholder.</li>\n<li>\n<strong>Browse library</strong><br>\nChoose a pre-built campaign from the campaigns library.</li>\n<li>\n<strong>Build your own</strong><br>\nBuilt a campaign from scratch.</li>\n<li>\n<strong>Delete placeholder</strong><br>\nRemove the selected placeholder from the calendar.<br>\n<p>Follow these guides for more information on creating campaigns:</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/115005054847\">How to create and send an email campaign</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/360040039971\">How to create and send an SMS campaign</a></li>\n</ul>",
    "user_segment_ids": []
  },
